desc: Mixed Messages (SWH Hermes Filter port) by chmaha
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
tags: filter ring modulator oscillator distortion delay swh
about:
  Mixed Messages: Steve Harris's Hermes Filter, a sound mangler built from two oscillators, two LFOs, three
  ring modulators and a three-band crossover, each band with its own distortion, modulated filter and delay. The
  input, both oscillators and three ring modulators (Osc 1 x Osc 2, Input x Osc 2, Osc 1 x Input) are mixed and soft
  clipped, then split at the two crossover frequencies into Band 1 (above the upper frequency), Band 2 (between) and
  Band 3 (below the lower frequency). Each band runs drive, a state-variable filter (LP, HP, BP, BR or AP, cutoff
  swept by both LFOs), a feedback delay of up to 2 s and a gain, and the bands are summed and soft clipped. Ring mod
  depth 0 passes the first signal at +6 dB, 1 is amplitude modulation and 2 is ring modulation. Stereo runs two
  identical engines, one per channel (only the noise oscillator differs between them).
  Drag a knob to change it, hold Shift for fine steps, use the mouse wheel, and double-click to reset.
  Ported from Steve Harris's swh-plugins, https://github.com/swh/lv2 (GPL-3). Upstream bugs fixed in this version:
  the filters never ran (so the filter section and both LFOs did nothing); every band used Band 1's drive in the
  distortion; LFO 2's sample-and-hold ran at LFO 1's rate, and both sample-and-hold LFOs ran 16 times slow; the noise
  oscillator and sample-and-hold only gave -1 to -0.5; the filter cutoff jumped at every audio block, so the sound
  depended on the block size; delay time 0 gave a 2 s echo (now no delay); the "3x oversampled" filters fed each pass
  back as the next input instead of oversampling, so the crossover and filters self-oscillated (now real 3x
  oversampling with an interpolated input). Drive defaults to 1 (about unity) rather than upstream's 0, which
  lowers and distorts the signal.
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
provides:
  Dependencies/MixedMessages/hermes_dsp.jsfx-inc

slider1:h_lfo1_freq=250<0,1000,0.01>-LFO 1 Frequency (Hz)
slider2:h_lfo1_wave=0<0,4,1{Sine,Triangle,Saw,Square,S&H}>-LFO 1 Waveform
slider3:h_lfo2_freq=250<0,1000,0.01>-LFO 2 Frequency (Hz)
slider4:h_lfo2_wave=0<0,4,1{Sine,Triangle,Saw,Square,S&H}>-LFO 2 Waveform
slider5:h_osc1_freq=440<0,4000,0.01>-Osc 1 Frequency (Hz)
slider6:h_osc1_wave=0<0,4,1{Sine,Triangle,Saw,Square,Noise}>-Osc 1 Waveform
slider7:h_osc2_freq=440<0,4000,0.01>-Osc 2 Frequency (Hz)
slider8:h_osc2_wave=0<0,4,1{Sine,Triangle,Saw,Square,Noise}>-Osc 2 Waveform
slider9:h_rm1_depth=0<0,2,0.001>-Ring Mod 1 Depth
slider10:h_rm2_depth=0<0,2,0.001>-Ring Mod 2 Depth
slider11:h_rm3_depth=0<0,2,0.001>-Ring Mod 3 Depth
slider12:h_osc1_gain_db=-70<-70,20,0.01>-Osc 1 Gain (dB)
slider13:h_rm1_gain_db=-70<-70,20,0.01>-Ring Mod 1 Gain (dB)
slider14:h_osc2_gain_db=-70<-70,20,0.01>-Osc 2 Gain (dB)
slider15:h_rm2_gain_db=-70<-70,20,0.01>-Ring Mod 2 Gain (dB)
slider16:h_in_gain_db=0<-70,20,0.01>-Input Gain (dB)
slider17:h_rm3_gain_db=-70<-70,20,0.01>-Ring Mod 3 Gain (dB)
slider18:h_xover_lfreqp=1537.5<50,6000,0.1>-Crossover Lower Frequency (Hz)
slider19:h_xover_ufreqp=7750<1000,10000,0.1>-Crossover Upper Frequency (Hz)
slider20:h_drive1=1<0,3,0.001>-Band 1 Drive
slider21:h_drive2=1<0,3,0.001>-Band 2 Drive
slider22:h_drive3=1<0,3,0.001>-Band 3 Drive
slider23:h_filt1_type=0<0,5,1{Off,LP,HP,BP,BR,AP}>-Band 1 Filter Type
